.TH VORTEX 1 "August 2026" "Linux Vortex Terminal 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
vortex \- local-first Linux cybersecurity and operations workbench
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B vortex
.RI [ options ] " request"
.br
.B vortex plan
.RI [ options ] " request"
.br
.B vortex run
.RI plan-id
.SH DESCRIPTION
Linux Vortex Terminal turns a natural-language objective into a typed, inspectable
plan. It probes the real tools installed on the host, requires explicit approval,
and executes through one local process authority. It never treats model text as
shell authority and never fabricates tool output or findings.
.PP
Active security operations require an authorized engagement and a declared scope.
Credential attacks, exploitation, persistence, evasion, malware, exfiltration,
denial of service, and unrestricted scanning are blocked.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.BR ask
Explain or diagnose without executing.
.TP
.BR plan
Create and print a saved plan without executing.
.TP
.BR doctor
Show factual Linux context and package/model availability.
.TP
.BR tools
Probe installed tools and versions.
.TP
.BR engagement
Create or list an authorization scope.
.TP
.BR run
Run one approved plan, or an explicitly attributed direct argv after `--`.
.TP
.BR shell
Preview or explicitly install/uninstall an idempotent Vortex-owned shell block.
The command never edits a shell startup file without explicit approval.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR --json
Write schema-versioned machine output.
.TP
.BR --cwd=DIR
Use DIR as the working-directory scope.
.TP
.BR --offline
Disable model and outbound capabilities.
.TP
.BR --non-interactive
Refuse unless exact plan digest and approval token are supplied.
.TP
.BR --allow-root
Explicitly allow one invocation as UID 0; no password is captured.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/vortex
Configuration, owner-only.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/vortex/vortex.db
Local SQLite history and audit events, owner-only.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 success, 1 general failure, 2 invalid usage, 3 unavailable, 4 policy denied,
5 confirmation required/declined, 6 command non-zero, 7 interrupted, 8 timeout,
9 integrity failure, and 10 incompatible state. See docs/EXIT_CODES.md.
.SH SECURITY
No automatic sudo, cloud model, telemetry, public listener, runtime plugin, or
remote-control mode is provided. Use only on systems and targets you are
authorized to administer or assess.
